# Restart the app only when the user will verify live

Do NOT restart the game at the end of every turn. The user is iterating quickly and
does not want the game relaunched after each small change or each test run.

## When to restart

Run `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/restart_app.ps1` from the project
root ONLY when:
- The user is about to verify the change in the running game and has just finished
  asking for it (e.g. "restart the game", "let me see it", "I'll check it now").
- A batch of related changes is complete and the user was waiting for them live.

## When NOT to restart

- After running a self-test / selftest harness run (those spawn their own Godot
  process and exit).
- After a code edit that has not been asked to be viewed live.
- Mid-plan, while there are still pending tasks to implement. Keep building;
  restart once when the batch is done and the user asks to look.
- Docs-only / question-only replies with zero code/asset edits.

If in doubt, do NOT restart — finish the remaining tasks first, then restart once.

Default launch is the normal bootstrap scene. Use `-Pjotr` or `-Classic` only when
the change is mode-specific.